;;; `open` written as an hrule's conclusion argument loads, and the hrule
;;; proposes a fact about it — M1f **W71**, register row `W71/hrule-value`,
;;; filed by S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.2, 2026-11-10).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `h` is an hrule whose conclusion is `(p open)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is the verdict a rule's `:assert` states, `(open)` or `(open ?R)`,
;;; and is written nowhere else (the user's ruling on Q-M1f.66, 2026-11-10):
;;; here it is written as an hrule's conclusion argument, so the program is
;;; refused at the parse, at the `open`, and every command exits 1 (`ein test`:
;;; 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, `h` proposes `(p open)`, and R is
;;; 2 states, ∅ and `{(p open)}`, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at the parse since S1f.5.23 (T1f.5.23.3).

(relation a Thing :why "{?1} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?1} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?1} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(hrule h ()
  :match  (a ?x)
  :assert (p open)
  :why "{?x} is an a, so open may be a p")
